  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 304.24 Certified Operator Notification and Reporting Responsibilities",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 304.24 Certified Operator Notification and Reporting Responsibilities.\n\n(a) Each operator who receives certification pursuant to these rules shall maintain a current mailing address, daytime telephone number, and email address, if available, on file with the department, at least one of which shall be for the operator personally rather than for the operator’s employer.\n\n(b) All communications issued by or at the direction of the department that are sent to the operator’s last address of record shall be presumed to have been received by the operator.\n\n(c) An operator shall notify the department in writing upon being designated as an OIRC, a back-up OIRC, or upon termination from such a position.\n\n(d) The OIRC shall annually complete and submit electronically to the department, no later than February 15, the \"Wastewater Operator in Responsible Charge Verification Form\", NHDES-W-09-055, September 2023, available at: https://onlineforms.nh.gov/?formtag=NHDES-W-09-055.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at part heading for Env-Wq 304) #10392, eff 8-1-13; ss by #13755, eff 9-27-23 (formerly Env-Wq 304.26) (see Revision Note #2 at part heading for Env-Wq 304)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq300.html"
